b/add "a129c702-2ff3-58b7-ad79-ebd1f5f5e3fd" :answer-field/choices "ca3b9214-ba37-554e-8f3a-6c36336e27f6"] [:db/add "a129c702-2ff3-58b7-ad79-ebd1f5f5e3fd" :answer-field/correct "ca3b9214-ba37-554e-8f3a-6c36336e27f6"] [:db/ensure "a129c702-2ff3-58b7-ad79-ebd1f5f5e3fd" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "a2de795b-e01a-5d1a-a0a1-efe2f159f8e8" :question/id #uuid "a2de795b-e01a-5d1a-a0a1-efe2f159f8e8"] [:db/add "a2de795b-e01a-5d1a-a0a1-efe2f159f8e8" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\sin\\theta-2\n$$\n\n$$\ny=-\\cos\\theta-1\n$$\n\n$$\n0\\le \\theta<2\\pi\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y$?\n\nThe range of $x$ is:\n\n{{field-1}} {{field-2}} $x\\le$ {{field-3}}.\n\nThe range of $y$ is:\n\n{{field-4}} $\\le y$ {{field-5}} {{field-6}}."] [:db/add "a2de795b-e01a-5d1a-a0a1-efe2f159f8e8" :question/worked-solution "Consider each coordinate separately.\n\nFor $x$:\n\nOver the full turn, $\\sin\\theta$ attains both $-1$ and $1$, including at permitted parameter values.\n\nMultiply by $1$ and translate by $-2$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &\\le \\sin\\theta\\le 1 \\\\\n-3 &\\le \\sin\\theta-2\\le -1 \\\\\n-3 &\\le x\\le -1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $-3\\le x\\le -1$.\n\nFor $y$:\n\nOver the full turn, $\\cos\\theta$ attains both $-1$ and $1$, including at permitted parameter values.\n\nMultiplying by $-1$ reverses both comparisons; translate by $-1$, then write the bounds in increasing order.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &\\le \\cos\\theta\\le 1 \\\\\n1 &\\ge-\\cos\\theta\\ge-1 \\\\\n0 &\\ge-\\cos\\theta-1\\ge-2 \\\\\n-2 &\\le y\\le 0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $-2\\le y\\le 0$.\n\nContinuity gives every value between the stated bounds. The coordinate extrema need not occur at the same parameter value."] [:db/add "a2de795b-e01a-5d1a-a0a1-efe2f159f8e8" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "a2de795b-e01a-5d1a-a0a1-efe2f159f8e8" :question/answer-fields "e5d28d2e-6c6c-5f21-9960-35c03c73c5e6"] [:db/add "a2de795b-e0