" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "c3056563-bedd-5679-a97d-6129732ad4ae" :answer-field/choices "698f89c3-9b78-5576-af7d-ee358f849071"] [:db/add "c3056563-bedd-5679-a97d-6129732ad4ae" :answer-field/correct "698f89c3-9b78-5576-af7d-ee358f849071"] [:db/ensure "c3056563-bedd-5679-a97d-6129732ad4ae" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "417b6422-5a3f-5388-bb37-751ac4cc3fcc" :answer/id #uuid "417b6422-5a3f-5388-bb37-751ac4cc3fcc"] [:db/add "417b6422-5a3f-5388-bb37-751ac4cc3fcc" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "417b6422-5a3f-5388-bb37-751ac4cc3fcc" :answer/value "1"] [:db/ensure "417b6422-5a3f-5388-bb37-751ac4cc3fcc" :answer/validate] [:db/add "3483224f-7594-5ef2-9812-406a6a970da3" :answer-field/id #uuid "3483224f-7594-5ef2-9812-406a6a970da3"] [:db/add "3483224f-7594-5ef2-9812-406a6a970da3" :answer-field/key "field-8"] [:db/add "3483224f-7594-5ef2-9812-406a6a970da3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "3483224f-7594-5ef2-9812-406a6a970da3" :answer-field/choices "417b6422-5a3f-5388-bb37-751ac4cc3fcc"] [:db/add "3483224f-7594-5ef2-9812-406a6a970da3" :answer-field/correct "417b6422-5a3f-5388-bb37-751ac4cc3fcc"] [:db/ensure "3483224f-7594-5ef2-9812-406a6a970da3" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "9be81fc9-7ca5-585d-82c8-4cef152879eb" :question/id #uuid "9be81fc9-7ca5-585d-82c8-4cef152879eb"] [:db/add "9be81fc9-7ca5-585d-82c8-4cef152879eb" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=3\\sin\\theta-2\n$$\n\n$$\ny=-3\\cos\\theta-2\n$$\n\n$$\n0\\le \\theta<\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y$? Use $<$ or $\\le$ in the comparison blanks.\n\nThe range of $x$ is:\n\n{{field-1}} {{field-2}} $x$ {{field-3}} {{field-4}}.\n\nThe range of $y$ is:\n\n{{field-5}} {{field-6}} $y$ {{field-7}} {{field-8}}."] [:db/add "9be81fc9-7ca5-585d-82c8-4cef152879eb" :question/worked-solution "Consider each coordinate separately.\n\nFor $x$:\n\nCheck the quarter-turn points in the parameter interval and its endpoint limits: $\\theta=0$ gives $\\sin\\theta=0$ (included); $\\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\sin\\theta=1$ (included); $\\theta=\\pi$ gives $\\sin\\theta=0$ (included); $\\theta=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\sin\\theta=-1$ (excluded endpoint).\n\nThe value $-1$ is approached at an excluded endpoint and is not attained elsewhere in the interval.\n\nThe value $1$ is attained at $\\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$.\n\nMultiply by $3$ and translate by $-2$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &<\\sin\\theta\\le 1 \\\\\n-3 &<3\\sin\\theta\\le 3 \\\\\n-5 &<3\\sin\\theta-2\\le 1 \\\\\n-5 &<x\\le 1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $-5<x\\le 1$.\n\nFor $y$:\n\nCheck the quarter-turn points in the parameter interval and its endpoint limits: $\\theta=0$ gives $\\cos\\theta=1$ (included); $\\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\cos\\theta=0$ (included); $\\theta=\\pi$ gives $\\cos\\theta=-1$ (included); $\\theta=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\cos\\theta=0$ (excluded endpoint).\n\nThe value $-1$ is attained at $\\theta=\\pi$.\n\nThe value $1$ is attained at $\\theta=0$.\n\nMultiplying by $-3$ reverses both comparisons; translate by $-2$, then write the bounds in increasing order.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &\\le \\cos\\theta\\le 1 \\\\\n3 &\\ge-3\\cos\\theta\\ge-3 \\\\\n1 &\\ge-3\\cos\\theta-2\\ge-5 \\\\\n-5 &\\le y\\le 1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $-5\\le y\\le 1$.\n\nContinuity gives every value between the stated bounds. The coordinate extrema need not occur at the same parameter value."] [:db/add "9be81fc9-7ca5-585d-82c8-4cef152879eb" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "9be81fc9-7ca5-585d-82c8-4cef152879eb" :question/answer-fields "d00e13cd-409e-5893-b570-7f72206c180a"] [:db/add "9be81fc9-7ca5-585d-82c8-4cef152879eb" :question/answer-fields "2cdad3c0-af7a-5fed-837d-c872fa25d755"] [:db/add "9be81fc9-7ca5-585d-82c8-4cef152879eb" :question/answer-fields "f4975167-f3cc-5ac7-b9c7-62d146db15c7"] [:db/add "9be81fc9-7ca5-585d-82c8-4cef152879eb" :question/answer-fields "1d7ea162-34c2-5030