curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=2\\sin\\theta-1\n$$\n\n$$\ny=-4\\cos\\theta-1\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\pi}{2}<\\theta<\\frac{5\\pi}{2}\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y$? Use $<$ or $\\le$ in the comparison blanks.\n\nThe range of $x$ is:\n\n{{field-1}} {{field-2}} $x$ {{field-3}} {{field-4}}.\n\nThe range of $y$ is:\n\n{{field-5}} {{field-6}} $y$ {{field-7}} {{field-8}}."] [:db/add "0845d3c8-57df-56fb-8a57-7e48473e3c7b" :question/worked-solution "Consider each coordinate separately.\n\nFor $x$:\n\nCheck the quarter-turn points in the parameter interval and its endpoint limits: $\\theta=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\sin\\theta=-1$ (excluded endpoint); $\\theta=2\\pi$ gives $\\sin\\theta=0$ (included); $\\theta=\\frac{5\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\sin\\theta=1$ (excluded endpoint).\n\nThe value $-1$ is approached at an excluded endpoint and is not attained elsewhere in the interval.\n\nThe value $1$ is approached at an excluded endpoint and is not attained elsewhere in the interval.\n\nMultiply by $2$ and translate by $-1$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &<\\sin\\theta<1 \\\\\n-2 &<2\\sin\\theta<2 \\\\\n-3 &<2\\sin\\theta-1<1 \\\\\n-3 &<x<1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $-3<x<1$.\n\nFor $y$:\n\nCheck the quarter-turn points in the parameter interval and its endpoint limits: $\\theta=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\cos\\theta=0$ (excluded endpoint); $\\theta=2\\pi$ gives $\\cos\\theta=1$ (included); $\\theta=\\frac{5\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\cos\\theta=0$ (excluded endpoint).\n\nThe value $0$ is approached at an excluded endpoint and is not attained elsewhere in the interval.\n\nThe value $1$ is attained at $\\theta=2\\pi$.\n\nMultiplying by $-4$ reverses both comparisons; translate by $-1$, then write the bounds in increasing order.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0 &<\\cos\\theta\\le 1 \\\\\n0 &>-4\\cos\\theta\\ge-4 \\\\\n-1 &>-4\\cos\\theta-1\\ge-5 \\\\\n-5 &\\le y<-1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $-5\\le y<-1$.\n\nContinuity gives every value between the stated bounds. The coordinate extrema need not occur at the same parameter value."] [:db/add "0845d3c8-57df-56fb-8a57-7e48473e3c7b" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "0845d3c8-57df-56fb-8a57-7e48473e3c7b" :question/answer-fields "11c526f1-c0ae-57e3-a463-b6ba66ee55de"] [:db/add "0845d3c8-57df-56fb-8a57-7e48473e3c7b" :question/answer-fields "74220090-825d-581e-b832-75a84b800169"] [:db/add "0845d3c8-57df-56fb-8a57-7e48473e3c7b" :question/answer-fields "6e0d9aba-b1cd-5fc5-9637-15da1d299fd7"] [:db/add "0845d3c8-57df-56fb-8a57-7e48473e3c7b" :question/answer-fields "cae2d10f-5daa-5ad5-aa42-c94aa1d0a25a"] [:db/add "0845d3c8-57df-56fb-8a57-7e48473e3c7b" :question/answer-fields "de5ccf0f-226a-5470-a761-228982a63535"] [:db/add "0845d3c8-57df-56fb-8a57-7e48473e3c7b" :question/answer-fields "a80bd821-e741-53f7-b8a0-cd78f37f3680"] [:db/add "0845d3c8-57df-56fb-8a57-7e48473e3c7b" :question/answer-fields "f3a4516e-bd90-556f-b9a7-70bdeea7c7f0"] [:db/add "0845d3c8-57df-56fb-8a57-7e48473e3c7b" :question/answer-fields "f66f6efa-f7a5-5c09-be30-878e9528055e"] [:db/ensure "0845d3c8-57df-56fb-8a57-7e48473e3c7b" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186087736 :knowledge-point/questions "0845d3c8-57df-56fb-8a57-7e48473e3c7b"] [:db/add "f7fda03f-4bbc-532a-b528-cf599918b057" :answer/id #uuid "f7fda03f-4bbc-532a-b528-cf599918b057"] [:db/add "f7fda03f-4bbc-532a-b528-cf599918b057" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "f7fda03f-4bbc-532a-b528-cf599918b057" :answer/value "-4"] [:db/ensure "f7fda03f-4bbc-532a-b528-cf599918b057" :answer/validate] [:db/add "e8b466a1-e158-54e7-998c-7e39eac58119" :answer-field/id #uuid "e8b466a1-e158-54e7-998c-7e39eac58119"] [:db/add "e8b466a1-e158-54e7-998c-7e39eac58119" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "e8b466a1-e158-54e7-998c-7e39eac58119" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "e8b466a1-e158-54e7-998c-7e39eac58119" :answer-field/choices "f7fda03f-4bbc-532a-b528-cf599918b057"] [:db/add "e8b466a1-e158-54e7-998c-7e39eac58119" :answer-field/correct "f7fda03f-