ld-8"] [:db/add "2d3171e6-c39f-5f57-aba9-431939386799" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "2d3171e6-c39f-5f57-aba9-431939386799" :answer-field/choices "92803794-9464-5558-8b24-c4229b6dedc6"] [:db/add "2d3171e6-c39f-5f57-aba9-431939386799" :answer-field/correct "92803794-9464-5558-8b24-c4229b6dedc6"] [:db/ensure "2d3171e6-c39f-5f57-aba9-431939386799" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "2935e5f4-7054-55f9-b43d-186688be6a4b" :question/id #uuid "2935e5f4-7054-55f9-b43d-186688be6a4b"] [:db/add "2935e5f4-7054-55f9-b43d-186688be6a4b" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=-2\\cos\\theta-2\n$$\n\n$$\ny=-4\\sin\\theta-1\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\pi}{2}<\\theta\\le \\frac{5\\pi}{2}\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y$? Use $<$ or $\\le$ in the comparison blanks.\n\nThe range of $x$ is:\n\n{{field-1}} {{field-2}} $x$ {{field-3}} {{field-4}}.\n\nThe range of $y$ is:\n\n{{field-5}} {{field-6}} $y$ {{field-7}} {{field-8}}."] [:db/add "2935e5f4-7054-55f9-b43d-186688be6a4b" :question/worked-solution "Consider each coordinate separately.\n\nFor $x$:\n\nCheck the quarter-turn points in the parameter interval and its endpoint limits: $\\theta=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\cos\\theta=0$ (excluded endpoint); $\\theta=2\\pi$ gives $\\cos\\theta=1$ (included); $\\theta=\\frac{5\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\cos\\theta=0$ (included).\n\nThe value $0$ is attained at $\\theta=\\frac{5\\pi}{2}$.\n\nThe value $1$ is attained at $\\theta=2\\pi$.\n\nMultiplying by $-2$ reverses both comparisons; translate by $-2$, then write the bounds in increasing order.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0 &\\le \\cos\\theta\\le 1 \\\\\n0 &\\ge-2\\cos\\theta\\ge-2 \\\\\n-2 &\\ge-2\\cos\\theta-2\\ge-4 \\\\\n-4 &\\le x\\le -2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $-4\\le x\\le -2$.\n\nFor $y$:\n\nCheck the quarter-turn points in the parameter interval and its endpoint limits: $\\theta=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\sin\\theta=-1$ (excluded endpoint); $\\theta=2\\pi$ gives $\\sin\\theta=0$ (included); $\\theta=\\frac{5\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\sin\\theta=1$ (included).\n\nThe value $-1$ is approached at an excluded endpoint and is not attained elsewhere in the interval.\n\nThe value $1$ is attained at $\\theta=\\frac{5\\pi}{2}$.\n\nMultiplying by $-4$ reverses both comparisons; translate by $-1$, then write the bounds in increasing order.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &<\\sin\\theta\\le 1 \\\\\n4 &>-4\\sin\\theta\\ge-4 \\\\\n3 &>-4\\sin\\theta-1\\ge-5 \\\\\n-5 &\\le y<3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $-5\\le y<3$.\n\nContinuity gives every value between the stated bounds. The coordinate extrema need not occur at the same parameter value."] [:db/add "2935e5f4-7054-55f9-b43d-186688be6a4b" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "2935e5f4-7054-55f9-b43d-186688be6a4b" :question/answer-fields "e8b466a1-e158-54e7-998c-7e39eac58119"] [:db/add "2935e5f4-7054-55f9-b43d-186688be6a4b" :question/answer-fields "76d957b4-189a-5f4a-ab4d-a4280433cd49"] [:db/add "2935e5f4-7054-55f9-b43d-186688be6a4b" :question/answer-fields "075c5c18-de0c-52fb-bd58-d3c4c41baa12"] [:db/add "2935e5f4-7054-55f9-b43d-186688be6a4b" :question/answer-fields "c7db34e5-a7dd-50d2-9d1f-d123ea91d1f7"] [:db/add "2935e5f4-7054-55f9-b43d-186688be6a4b" :question/answer-fields "644f71ab-6c4d-587f-a3d9-fb2630d111c2"] [:db/add "2935e5f4-7054-55f9-b43d-186688be6a4b" :question/answer-fields "96a98e07-4422-59cd-9df7-151f2092ad9c"] [:db/add "2935e5f4-7054-55f9-b43d-186688be6a4b" :question/answer-fields "fdfc98af-86b7-522a-8de4-3fe92febf132"] [:db/add "2935e5f4-7054-55f9-b43d-186688be6a4b" :question/answer-fields "2d3171e6-c39f-5f57-aba9-431939386799"] [:db/ensure "2935e5f4-7054-55f9-b43d-186688be6a4b" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186087736 :knowledge-point/questions "2935e5f4-7054-55f9-b43d-186688be6a4b"] [:db/add "52a95556-56a2-5ef2-a63e-fd5c2f7ee49c" :answer/id #uuid "52a95556-56a2-5ef2-a63e-fd5c2f7ee49c"] [:db/add "52a95556-56a2-5ef2-a63e-fd5c2f7ee49c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "52a95