 of $x$ is:\n\n{{field-1}} {{field-2}} $x$ {{field-3}} {{field-4}}.\n\nThe range of $y$ is:\n\n{{field-5}} {{field-6}} $y$ {{field-7}} {{field-8}}."] [:db/add "6d58730a-cc4d-57f4-9e65-fe850ab7f690" :question/worked-solution "Consider each coordinate separately.\n\nFor $x$:\n\nCheck the quarter-turn points in the parameter interval and its endpoint limits: $\\theta=0$ gives $\\cos\\theta=1$ (excluded endpoint); $\\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\cos\\theta=0$ (included); $\\theta=\\pi$ gives $\\cos\\theta=-1$ (included); $\\theta=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\cos\\theta=0$ (excluded endpoint).\n\nThe value $-1$ is attained at $\\theta=\\pi$.\n\nThe value $1$ is approached at an excluded endpoint and is not attained elsewhere in the interval.\n\nMultiplying by $-4$ reverses both comparisons; translate by $2$, then write the bounds in increasing order.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &\\le \\cos\\theta<1 \\\\\n4 &\\ge-4\\cos\\theta>-4 \\\\\n6 &\\ge-4\\cos\\theta+2>-2 \\\\\n-2 &<x\\le 6.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $-2<x\\le 6$.\n\nFor $y$:\n\nCheck the quarter-turn points in the parameter interval and its endpoint limits: $\\theta=0$ gives $\\sin\\theta=0$ (excluded endpoint); $\\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\sin\\theta=1$ (included); $\\theta=\\pi$ gives $\\sin\\theta=0$ (included); $\\theta=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\sin\\theta=-1$ (excluded endpoint).\n\nThe value $-1$ is approached at an excluded endpoint and is not attained elsewhere in the interval.\n\nThe value $1$ is attained at $\\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$.\n\nMultiplying by $-2$ reverses both comparisons; translate by $-3$, then write the bounds in increasing order.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &<\\sin\\theta\\le 1 \\\\\n2 &>-2\\sin\\theta\\ge-2 \\\\\n-1 &>-2\\sin\\theta-3\\ge-5 \\\\\n-5 &\\le y<-1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $-5\\le y<-1$.\n\nContinuity gives every value between the stated bounds. The coordinate extrema need not occur at the same parameter value."] [:db/add "6d58730a-cc4d-57f4-9e65-fe850ab7f690" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "6d58730a-cc4d-57f4-9e65-fe850ab7f690" :question/answer-fields "c7dcb64e-fd77-5ef0-80a1-2fe2a1474c13"] [:db/add "6d58730a-cc4d-57f4-9e65-fe850ab7f690" :question/answer-fields "a89a39aa-550d-5b6d-9178-cc241c468ac1"] [:db/add "6d58730a-cc4d-57f4-9e65-fe850ab7f690" :question/answer-fields "ace2fc3a-9732-5630-8369-f8d0a7a32af3"] [:db/add "6d58730a-cc4d-57f4-9e65-fe850ab7f690" :question/answer-fields "c99ad0b2-0339-5c5a-94b6-e4ece3171312"] [:db/add "6d58730a-cc4d-57f4-9e65-fe850ab7f690" :question/answer-fields "054be713-d096-5722-baf0-09f64983bf3e"] [:db/add "6d58730a-cc4d-57f4-9e65-fe850ab7f690" :question/answer-fields "e06dde14-a30a-53f1-828f-0910cbb3f095"] [:db/add "6d58730a-cc4d-57f4-9e65-fe850ab7f690" :question/answer-fields "39348a04-463d-5342-bd4b-15d8cad5289f"] [:db/add "6d58730a-cc4d-57f4-9e65-fe850ab7f690" :question/answer-fields "d7ae3133-656c-5bb5-9da0-f4ff80734ba0"] [:db/ensure "6d58730a-cc4d-57f4-9e65-fe850ab7f690" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186087736 :knowledge-point/questions "6d58730a-cc4d-57f4-9e65-fe850ab7f690"] [:db/add "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "d3491f91-56ba-5456-be4c-e393b1ae8052"] [:db/add "generator" :question-generator/script "generators/e2/e2478e678f31b037427dc6d99ace378950f184639a80db63b16798d5a178202e/generator.py"] [:db/add 17592186087736 :knowledge-point/question-generator "generator"] [:db/ensure 17592186087736 :knowledge-point/validate] [:db/cas 17592186526245 :question/retired nil true] [:db/cas 17592186526250 :question/retired nil true] [:db/cas 17592186526255 :question/retired nil true] [:db/cas 17592186526260 :question/retired nil true] [:db/cas 17592186526264 :question/retired nil true] [:db/cas 17592186698065 :question/retired nil true] [:db/cas 17592186698070 :question/retired nil true] [:db/cas 17592186698072 :question/retired nil true] [:db/cas 17592186698224 :question/retired nil true] [:db/cas 17592186698228 :question/retired nil true] [:db/cas 17592186